---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About &amp; Transparency — HubHum"
  description="How HubHum works, who maintains it, how AI summaries are validated, what Verified Official Links guarantee, and how #ad partner links stay strictly separated."
>
  <div class="container detail-wrap">
    <a href={withBase('/')} class="breadcrumb">← Back to HubHum Catalog</a>

    <section class="article-card" style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
      <div class="hero-badge" style="margin-bottom:0.85rem;">
        <span>Independent Directory • Editorial &amp; Affiliate Transparency</span>
      </div>
      <h1 style="margin:0 0 0.5rem;font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.1rem);">
        About HubHum &amp; How This Directory Works
      </h1>
      <p style="margin:0 0 1.4rem;color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.92rem;">
        Updated: <strong>{lastUpdated}</strong> • Plain-English Open-Source Software Guide
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.4rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        1. Who Runs HubHum
      </h2>
      <p>
        HubHum (<em>&ldquo;A Git Hub for Humans&rdquo;</em>) is an independent open-source software catalog built and maintained by{' '}
        <strong>Keoma Davanzo</strong> via the public repository{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/DavanzoKeoma/HubHum"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          style="color:var(--accent-fg-text);text-decoration:underline;"
        >
          DavanzoKeoma/HubHum
        </a>.
        HubHum is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by GitHub, Inc. or the individual maintainers of the open-source tools listed here.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.6rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        2. How Guides Are Generated (AI-Assisted + Automated Validation)
      </h2>
      <p>
        Many great open-source tools are hidden behind developer jargon. To explain software simply for everyday people:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Public GitHub Source Material:</strong> Every guide starts from public GitHub metadata, upstream{' '}
          <code>README</code> documentation, official project homepages, and public release assets.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI-Assisted Summarization:</strong> Plain-English descriptions and multilingual summaries (EN, IT, ES, FR, DE)
          are drafted with AI language models and structured into consistent sections (<em>What it does</em>,{' '}
          <em>Who it&apos;s for</em>, <em>Key features</em>, <em>How to install</em>, and <em>Pros and Cons</em>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deterministic Sanity Checks:</strong> Every published card passes automated validation scripts to prevent
          broken links, invented claims, missing licenses, or mixed promotional copy before deployment. Because active projects
          release updates frequently, always verify the latest install steps on the linked upstream GitHub repository.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.6rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        3. What &ldquo;Verified Official Links&rdquo; Means (and Does Not Mean)
      </h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Direct Upstream Routing Only:</strong> Every primary download button and{' '}
          <strong>Official Page</strong> link resolves strictly to the software author&apos;s official GitHub Releases page,
          GitHub repository (shown explicitly as <code>owner/repo</code> on each sheet), or verified project domain. HubHum
          never re-uploads binaries, wraps installers with adware, or serves third-party mirrors.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Clear Format Labels:</strong> Tools are separated by how you run them:{' '}
          <strong>Desktop App</strong> (standard installer), <strong>Self-Hosted App</strong> (Docker or server software you run yourself),{' '}
          <strong>CLI Tool</strong> (terminal utility without a graphical window), <strong>Cloud Web App</strong>, and{' '}
          <strong>Open Reference</strong> (curated guides or awesome-lists).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Local Security / Antivirus Guarantee:</strong> Automated URL verification confirms that links point to the authentic
          upstream project, not that a third-party repository is bug-free or audited by an antivirus lab. Always follow your
          operating system&apos;s security best practices before executing binaries or terminal commands.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.6rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        4. Affiliate &amp; <code>#ad</code> Funding Isolation
      </h2>
      <p>
        HubHum is free to browse, requires zero account sign-up, and sets zero tracking cookies. To help cover hosting and
        maintenance costs cleanly:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Strict Isolation:</strong> Affiliate links (tagged with <code>#ad</code> and{' '}
          <code>rel=&quot;sponsored noopener noreferrer&quot;</code>) are strictly isolated inside the dedicated{' '}
          <strong>Sponsored Partner Tools (#ad)</strong> section at the bottom of guides and the clearly labeled{' '}
          <strong>Sponsored Partner (#ad)</strong> sidebar card.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero Editorial Interference:</strong> Affiliate links are never injected into{' '}
          <em>What it does in plain English</em>, <em>Key features</em>, <em>How to install</em>, or official open-source download buttons.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:1.6rem;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
        5. Contact, Corrections &amp; Takedowns
      </h2>
      <p>
        Spotted an outdated description, misclassified tool, or broken official link? Open an issue or pull request on{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/DavanzoKeoma/HubHum/issues"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          style="color:var(--accent-fg-text);text-decoration:underline;"
        >
          DavanzoKeoma/HubHum Issues
        </a>{' '}
        or contact <code>keomadavanzo@gmail.com</code>. You can also review our{' '}
        <a
          href={withBase('/privacy/')}
          style="color:var(--accent-fg-text);text-decoration:underline;"
        >
          Privacy Policy
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
